## Windows Event Log ✅ (already connected)

Windows' built-in logging system — every significant thing that happens on the OS gets recorded here in three main channels:

| Channel | What it logs |
|---|---|
| **Application** | App crashes, app-level errors/warnings |
| **Security** | Logins, logouts, failed passwords, privilege changes |
| **System** | Driver issues, service start/stop, hardware events |

### How to check it yourself (outside Wazuh)

```powershell
# Open the built-in Event Viewer GUI
eventvwr.msc
```

Or from PowerShell directly:
```powershell
# Last 10 Security events
Get-WinEvent -LogName Security -MaxEvents 10

# Last 10 System events
Get-WinEvent -LogName System -MaxEvents 10
```

### How to check what Wazuh is reading

```powershell
type "C:\Program Files (x86)\ossec-agent\ossec.log" | findstr "event log"
```

This confirms the agent is actively watching those 3 channels — which we already saw is working.

